\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Awake, my Soul, And With The Sun
\par Thy daily stage of duty run;
\par Shake off dull sloth, and joyful rise,
\par To pay thy morning sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Redeem thy misspent moments past,
\par And live this day as if thy last;
\par Thy talents to improve take care;
\par For the great day thyself prepare.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let all thy converse be sincere,
\par Thy conscience as the noonday clear;
\par For God's all- seeing eye surveys,
\par Thy secret thoughts, thy words and ways.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Wake, and lift up thyself, my heart,
\par And with the angels bear thy part,
\par Who all night long unwearied sing
\par High praise to the eternal King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. All praise to Thee, who safe  hast kept;
\par And hast refreshed me whilst I slept,
\par Grant, Lord, when I from death shall wake,
\par I may of endless life partake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Lord, I my vows to Thee renew,
\par Disperse my sins as morning dew;
\par Guard my first springs of thought and will
\par And with Thyself my spirit fill.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Direct, control, suggest, this day,
\par All I design, or do, or say,
\par That all my powers, with all their might,
\par In Thy sole glory may unite.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Praise God, from whom all blessing flow;
\par Praise Him, all creatures here below;
\par Praise Him above, ye heavenly host;
\par Praise Father, Son, and Holy Ghost.
\par                                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

